{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>The bird of prey.</b> It is a bird — called so because it swoops and plunges toward carcasses to snatch food, as in ״וַתַּעַט אֶל הַשָּׁלָל״ (I Samuel 15)." "<b>Upon the carcasses.</b> Upon the pieces. הַפְּגָרִים is translated פַּגְלַיָּא, but because they were accustomed to translate ״אִישׁ בִּתְרוֹ״ as וִיהַב פַּלְגַּיָּא, the word פַּגְלַיָּא got confused for them into פַּלְגַּיָּא, and they translated הַפְּגָרִים as פַּלְגַּיָּא. And anyone who translates thus errs, because בְּתָרִים — its translation is פַּלְגַּיָּא, but פְּגָרִים — its translation is פַּגְלַיָּא, the term פִּגּוּל, as in ״פִּגּוּל הוּא״ (Leviticus 7) — the term for a carcass." "<b>And he sat.</b> A term of driving away and making fly off, as in ״יַשֵּׁב רוּחוֹ״ (Psalms 147) — a hint that David son of Jesse would come to destroy them, and they do not let him rest from heaven until King Messiah comes."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:49.945578666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}